## System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-3570K CPU @ 3.40GHz (4 threads) - 15.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nTest project has two labels, both have the same text having a soft hyphen in the middle. First label is using Roboto typeface, the second is using Platypi typeface, both fonts are from Google Fonts.\n\nBoth labels are wrapped as expected, but the label using Platypi doesn't show the hyphen.\n\n<img width=\"1621\" height=\"972\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e844ab21-00d6-4266-8597-db5d569fbd5c\" />\n\nMy (not very strong) understanding is that a typeface may contain a glyph for the soft hyphen (`00AD`) and in that case renderer should use that glyph when soft hyphen becomes visible. If the typeface doesn't contain a soft hyphen glyph, it should be replaced by the actual hyphen (`002D`). I don't know if this should be done automatically or using the typefaces cmap (Character to Glyph Index Mapping) table or by some other method. I wonder if Godot could use the actual hyphen glyph (`002D`) in case it seems that typeface itself doesn't contain any information how the soft hyphen should be drawn.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse reproduction project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[soft-hyphen-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21313803/soft-hyphen-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"http